Final Report: Axis Data Component

The axis component of the Data Visualization Library manages and displays axis information. It stores the minimum and maximum values, axis label, tick positions, and corresponding labels.

The AxisData class uses setter functions to update axis information and getter functions to retrieve stored values. The setRange() function validates the range before updating it.

The scaleValue() function normalizes a given value to a range between 0 and 1 using the axis minimum and maximum values. The printAxis() function displays the axis name, range, tick positions, and labels in the terminal.

The component is organized into a header file (axis.hpp), an implementation file (axis.cpp), and an example program (axis_example.cpp) used to test its functionality.

Overall, the component provides a structured and reusable way to manage axis data and perform basic axis scaling within the Data Visualization Library.
